# Line endings. Every text file in the repository is stored with LF; this file
# makes that hold regardless of how a checkout is configured.
#
# WHY. A copy of this repo made on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) and unpacked on
# Linux arrived with CRLF in every text file, and git reported 308 modified
# files -- ~2.8M lines "changed" with no content difference, including the
# large tables under dataset/raw/. With `text=auto`, git normalises line
# endings before comparing, so a CRLF working copy no longer reads as modified
# and a CRLF file cannot be committed as such.
#
# Windows checkouts still get CRLF in the working tree if they ask for it;
# only what is stored in the repository is fixed.
* text=auto

# Binary formats: never line-ending-normalised or text-diffed. Listed
# explicitly rather than trusting auto-detection, since a mangled byte in any
# of these corrupts the file silently. The first group is tracked today; the
# rest are formats this project produces or handles and may track later.
*.png       binary
*.npz       binary
*.cbm       binary
*.tfevents* binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.pdf       binary
*.npy       binary
*.pkl       binary
*.pt        binary
*.pth       binary
*.nii       binary
*.nii.gz    binary
*.gz        binary
*.zip       binary
*.tar       binary
